# DOC-pm: ROADMAP.oot as progress against NORTHSTAR

| Field | Value |
|-------|--------|
| **Paper ID** | `DOC-pm` |
| **Subject document(s)** | monorepo `ROADMAP.oot` |
| **Status** | `draft` |
| **Series** | Documentation system (`DOC-*`) |

## 1. Why this document exists

ROADMAP.oot is project management and execution roadmap: pin, full NORTHSTAR leaf checklist with honest status keys, milestone summary, rails, residual index. It answers how far without becoming a noisy sprint board.

## 2. Problem statement

PROGRESS went stale; PROJECT over-checked NORTHSTAR items. Two status docs fought. Agents and the website need one NORTHSTAR-aligned progress tracker.

## 3. Related work (university + commercial)

- Requirements traceability matrices (requirements engineering).
- Product roadmap / coverage matrices.
- Scrum product backlog as ordered product needs (not sprint commitment). https://scrumguides.org/scrum-guide.html
- Living documentation — status must be cheap to update or it lies.

## 4. Rationale for openOODA

Status keys: done | partial | smoke | residual | not-started. Row IDs (1.2, 3.6, …) shared with RP papers.

## 5. Limits and failure modes

Monorepo-local unless published. Tip can lag mid-cycle. Not a residual deep-dive substitute.

## 6. Alternatives considered

Wiki-only, issue-tracker-only, single mega-README, or oral tradition — all fail multi-agent continuity or honesty. Prefer git-versioned markdown with clear roles.

## 7. Reality (honesty)

ROADMAP is the active tracker; PROGRESS/PROJECT are stubs. Site summarizes ROADMAP.

## 8. Open questions

1. Publish ROADMAP on GH org?
2. Auto-generate site tables from ROADMAP?

## 9. Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Every NORTHSTAR leaf has a ROADMAP row.
- [ ] No false `done` for free/JIT/hive without product proof.

